  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday through Tuesday)\nIssued at 1225 AM CST Wed Nov 11 2026\n\nThe weather pattern becomes a bit more active as we move into this \nweekend and next week. A stout upper wave is set to barrel through \nthe region Saturday night and Sunday bringing widespread rain \nchances. Synoptic uncertainty is high due to varying tracks for the \nupper low, with a minority (~10%) of ensemble members keeping the \nrain footprint entirely southwest of our forecast area; and on the \nother end, 90th percentile values have 2-3 inches possible at any \npoint in our forecast area. A few embedded thunderstorms may be \npossible, but instability may be a limiting factor.\n\nThat uncertainty will translate into the temperature forecast as \nwell (particularly on Sunday). We're likely looking at 50s and 60s \non Saturday; 40s to 60s on Sunday. Low temperatures may approach \nfreezing in northern Oklahoma over the weekend (10-25th percentile), \nbut most members keep us above that threshold (and none have \nfreezing temps coinciding with precipitation right now).\n\nAs rain chances move out early Monday, we'll see at least a brief \ndry period with gradual warming before we transition to more \nsouthwesterly flow around mid week.\n\nDay",
